<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  com.atlas.capture — the Atlas OUTBOUND-only capture daemon (Echo + Quill, Phase 3).

  This launchd LaunchAgent runs the Swift capture app at login and keeps it alive.
  The daemon authenticates OUTBOUND and PULLS work from the cloud command endpoint
  (/capture/poll + /capture/ack); the laptop has ZERO inbound port. This plist therefore
  declares NO inbound-listener key of any kind — launchd does NOT open any port on the
  daemon's behalf.

  Privacy invariants (T-03-04-01 through T-03-04-05):
    - ZERO inbound listener keys anywhere in this file (outbound-only daemon, T-03-04-01).
    - Daemon initiates ALL connections; uses default cert validation on outbound HTTPS.
    - OAuth bearer token is stored in the macOS Keychain (Auth.swift: SecItemCopyMatching /
      SecItemAdd) — NEVER in this plist's EnvironmentVariables, never in UserDefaults.
    - Raw audio/screen never leave the device except as owner-approved derived artifacts.

  SECRETS are NOT in this file. The OAuth bearer token comes from the macOS Keychain,
  not from an EnvironmentVariables block. This is the key difference from com.atlas.bridge
  which used ATLAS_BRIDGE_TOKEN in EnvironmentVariables for the Node env — the Swift app
  reads the token directly from Keychain (T-03-04-02).

  Three changes from com.atlas.bridge.plist (per plan + PATTERNS.md):
    1. Label   → com.atlas.capture  (separate launchd agent; bridge is com.atlas.bridge)
    2. ProgramArguments → the built Swift binary (not Node)
    3. StandardOut/ErrorPath → new log paths

  Everything else (RunAtLoad, KeepAlive, no inbound listener keys) is PRESERVED verbatim.

  Install (owner go-live gate — after Developer-ID signing + notarization, D3-03):
    cp capture/com.atlas.capture.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.atlas.capture.plist
    launchctl load ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.atlas.capture.plist
  Owner verifies: lsof -i -nP | grep LISTEN  →  NO AtlasCapture port (gating criterion).

  NOTE: The binary path uses a placeholder USERNAME — the owner edits this to match their
  install location before registering the plist.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- Change 1: separate Label (com.atlas.bridge is the Node bridge; this is the Swift daemon) -->
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.atlas.capture</string>

  <!-- Change 2: ProgramArguments points at the built Swift binary, not Node.
       The owner edits USERNAME to match their home directory.
       Release build: swift build -c release in capture/ produces AtlasCapture. -->
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/Users/USERNAME/Atlas/capture/.build/release/AtlasCapture</string>
  </array>

  <!-- Start at login and restart if it exits (a dead daemon = missed meetings/forms).
       This plist has ZERO inbound-listener keys (T-03-04-01 — outbound-only daemon). -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- Change 3: new log paths (separate from com.atlas.bridge logs) -->
  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/atlas-capture.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/atlas-capture.err.log</string>

  <!-- SECRETS NOT IN THIS FILE (T-03-04-02).
       The OAuth bearer token is stored in the macOS Keychain and read by Auth.swift
       via SecItemCopyMatching. No EnvironmentVariables secret block here. -->
</dict>
</plist>
